  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercise_type\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"The concept of 'slow travel' is gaining popularity among tourists who want to experience a destination more deeply. Slow travel involves staying in one place for an extended period, usually between two weeks and several months, and immersing oneself in the local culture. This approach allows visitors to develop a better understanding of the community's daily life, traditions, and values.\n\nOne of the main advantages of slow travel is that it reduces the environmental impact of tourism. By staying in one place for an extended period, tourists can avoid the carbon footprint associated with frequent flights and transportation. Additionally, slow travel promotes cultural exchange and mutual understanding between visitors and locals.\n\nHowever, some critics argue that slow travel can also have negative consequences, such as over-tourism in certain areas. They claim that prolonged stays in popular destinations can lead to strain on local resources and infrastructure. Nevertheless, proponents of slow travel believe that it offers a more authentic and enriching experience for both visitors and locals.\n\nIn recent years, many tour operators have begun to offer slow travel packages that cater to this growing demand. These packages often include homestays, language classes, and cultural activities that allow tourists to engage with the local community in meaningful ways.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the article?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Slow travel reduces the environmental impact of tourism.\", \"Slow travel promotes over-tourism in popular destinations.\", \"Slow travel involves staying in one place for an extended period to experience local culture.\", \"Slow travel is a new concept that has been introduced recently.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"option3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"According to the article, what is one of the main advantages of slow travel?\",\n      \"options\": [\"It promotes cultural exchange and mutual understanding.\", \"It reduces the environmental impact of tourism.\", \"It allows visitors to experience a destination superficially.\", \"It encourages tourists to visit multiple destinations in a short period.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"option2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"The word 'homestays' in the article most likely refers to:\",\n      \"options\": [\"a type of accommodation that is environmentally friendly.\", \"a type of cultural activity that involves learning a local language.\", \"a type of accommodation where tourists stay with local families.\", \"a type of transportation service that connects tourists to popular destinations.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"option3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"What can be inferred about the author's attitude towards slow travel?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The author is skeptical and critical of slow travel.\", \"The author believes that slow travel has no benefits.\", \"The author thinks that slow travel offers a more authentic experience for both visitors and locals.\", \"The author has never tried slow travel before.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"option3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"According to the article, what is one of the potential drawbacks of slow travel?\",\n      \"options\": [\"It can lead to over-tourism in certain areas.\", \"It can cause strain on local resources and infrastructure.\", \"It can result in a loss of cultural identity for local communities.\", \"It can increase the environmental impact of tourism.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"option1\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
